<newsitem itemid="414305" id="root" date="1997-03-03" xml:lang="en">
<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Rebhold H1 shr surges, declares maiden div.</title>
<headline>Rebhold H1 shr surges, declares maiden div.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)	14.5	vs    9.6</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		   2.5	vs    nil</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   15.45	vs    10.28</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   20.13	vs    13.23</p>
<p>    Tax			  4.39	vs    2.82</p>
<p>    Interest received	0.71	vs    0.83</p>
<p>    Turnover		 365.20	vs    266.02</p>
<p>Div payment to be advised</p>
<p>on register March 20</p>
<p>Full name: Rebhold Ltd (beverages, hotels and leisure)</p>
<p>NOTE - The group said that earnings for the second half of the year should be higher than those in the first half.</p>
<p>Shareholders would be given the option of capitalisation shares in lieu of the dividend. Details would be announced on March 17 and posted on March 27.</p>
<p>It repeated its February 18 cautionary announcement that it was engaged in negotiations which could affect share prices.</p>
<p>-- Cape Town newsroom +27 21 25-2238</p>
</text>
